# 3\. PostgreSQL database design

I recommend organizing the database into six logical groups.

Database structure

1. Organization – factories, users, roles and permissions
2. Master data – products, raw materials, customers, suppliers, machines
3. Operations – production, consumption, dispatch, receipts
4. Inventory – stock ledger, stock balances, adjustments
5. Transfers – inter-factory dispatch and receiving
6. Documents and audit – bills, files, approvals and history

